<data name="AboutUTAU" xml:space="preserve"><value>About UTAU</value></data>
<data name="AboutUTAUDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>This plugin reads the oto.ini of a UTAU voicebank as it is and resynthesises it with WORLD. Single kana, VCV and CVVC voicebanks are all supported.</value></data>
<data name="AboutUTAUHowTo" xml:space="preserve"><value>Put the voicebank folders under user/resources/utau or add them to the search folders. The pronunciation is written in kana.</value></data>
<data name="AboutUTAUNotation" xml:space="preserve"><value>Writing &lt;!note:length&gt; in the pronunciation sets the pitch and the length of the kana that follows it. The length is written in milliseconds or as a note such as 1/4.</value></data>
<data name="AboutUTAUNotationExample" xml:space="preserve"><value>Example: &lt;!C4:1/4&gt;ど&lt;!D4&gt;れ&lt;!E4&gt;み  A rest is written as &lt;!R:200&gt;.</value></data>
<data name="AboutUTAUCredit" xml:space="preserve"><value>WorldNet, a port of WORLD by M. Morise, is used for the analysis and the synthesis.</value></data>
<data name="NoteEditorHint" xml:space="preserve"><value>Drag a note vertically to change its pitch and drag its right edge to change its length. Ctrl with the wheel zooms, Shift with the wheel scrolls sideways and Alt releases the snapping.</value></data>
<data name="NoteLyricDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>The alias of the oto.ini can also be written here directly.</value></data>
<data name="NoteVelocityDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Scales the length of the consonant. 100 keeps the original length and the factor is 2^((100-value)/100).</value></data>
<data name="NoteFollowOtoDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>A value of 0 uses the value declared in the oto.ini.</value></data>
<data name="NoteStartPointDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Moves the point where the source sample starts being read forward by this amount.</value></data>
